index 00000000..64c84a53
--- /dev/null
+++ b/CREALITY_HI_CFS_PATCH.md
@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+# Creality Hi / CFS source port for OrcaSlicer 2.5.0-beta
+
+Base: `345efec64c7b95a05ce5cf96df0dde66a158835c` (official v2.5.0-beta).
+
+Preserves the Creality device-page bridge, CFS sync/edit/feed/retract, external spool mapping,
+camera recovery, flush-volume metadata, and Hi 0.4/0.6 profiles from the 2.4.2 patch.
+Keeps 2.5 lazy webview recreation, script-handler tracking, missing-connection translations,
+the new filament-list refresh, shared Creality LAN discovery model table, K1 text frames
+and heartbeat acknowledgements, and the refactored timelapse generator.
+
+Default and Fast purge multipliers are baked into the exported flush matrix exactly once.
+Both exported multiplier arrays are normalized for Creality hosts. Timelapse Off also
+guards the new shared generator. Browser recreation reinstalls the Creality page scripts.
+
+Source application is not a hardware or binary compatibility certification. Build and run
+the installer round-trip checks, then validate on a Creality Hi/CFS before publishing.
+The bundled web assets must match the pinned 2.4.2 payload manifest; older core binaries
+must never be used as the 2.5 payload.
+
+Also preserves beta async WebSocket deadlines, command batching, layer-change placeholders and no-reload tab selection.
